"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThe work begins with a scene where the protagonist wakes up smelling blood in his house.  \nMemory from the previous night is cut off, and his whole body is covered in blood.  \nGoing downstairs, he finds the body of his mother, who was murdered with her throat slit by a razor.  \nIn the terrible situation, only one thought dominates his head:   \n\nIn this situation, the reader follows the protagonist in inferring the culprit amidst confusion and fear.  \n\nThis work explores pure evil itself.  \nI think it's a book that approaches the theme of , which Jeong You-jeong has consistently dug into, at the most profound and fundamental level.  \n\nPersonally, the process of finding the truth along with the reader from a first-person perspective and the shocking truth remain in my memory.  "